            <ArticleTitle>Naloxegol for managing opioid-induced constipation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>51-53</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.JAA.0000522146.29435.c7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Naloxegol is a peripherally acting mu-opioid receptor antagonist for opioid-induced constipation in adults with chronic noncancer pain. This drug's once-daily oral formulation can be used as monotherapy and helps to decrease the constipating effects of opioid therapy; however, it has been associated with abdominal pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
